"The critical Ising model on trees, concave recursions and nonlinear capacity (https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0503137)\nciteturn1academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 21.6 years ago; Authors: Robin Pemantle, Yuval Peres ... In particular, on a spherically symmetric tree that has $n^{\\alpha}b^n$ vertices at level $n$ (up to bounded factors), we prove that there is a unique Gibbs measure for the ferromagnetic Ising model at the relevant critical temperature if and only if $\\alpha\\le1/2$.\nTitle: The critical Ising model on trees, concave recursions and nonlinear capacity\nAuthors: Robin Pemantle, Yuval Peres\nDate: Tue Mar  8 09:36:15 2005\n\nWe consider the Ising model on a general tree under various boundary conditions: all plus, free and spin-glass. In each case, we determine when the root is influenced by the boundary values in the limit as the boundary recedes to infinity. We obtain exact capacity criteria that govern behavior at critical temperatures. For plus boundary conditions, an $L^3$ capacity arises. In particular, on a spherically symmetric tree that has $n^{\\alpha}b^n$ vertices at level $n$ (up to bounded factors), we prove that there is a unique Gibbs measure for the ferromagnetic Ising model at the relevant critical temperature if and only if $\\alpha\\le1/2$. Our proofs are based on a new link between nonlinear recursions on trees and $L^p$ capacities.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n(PDF) The critical Ising model on trees, concave recursions and nonlinear capacity (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/2118267_The_critical_Ising_model_on_trees_concave_recursions_and_nonlinear_capacity)\nciteturn1search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 16.7 years ago; Crawled: 5 months ago; THE CRITICAL ISING MODEL ON TREES 3 ... Recursions on trees and potential theory. ... Pemantle and Steif (1999) analyzed the Heisenberg ... Berger, N.,Kenyon, C.,Mossel, E. and Peres, Y. ... In 42nd IEEE Symposium on Foundations of